From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Doe <john.doe@somewhere.on.planet>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] JM10: arm the DW watchdog before booting the kernel

The JM10 kernel currently hangs during PCIe3.0 probe (before the USB
CDC console or pstore comes up), leaving a dead board and no trace. To
make such early hangs recoverable, arm the DW watchdog (WDT0 at
0xfeaf0000, 24 MHz tick, TORR=15 ~= 89 s) right before booting the
kernel. A hang then ends in a warm reset, which preserves DDR and the
ramoops/pstore log at 0x110000; on the next boot, holding VOL+ enters
U-Boot download mode and do_board_download() copies that log to eMMC
for host-side analysis.

The Linux DW watchdog driver (CONFIG_DW_WATCHDOG=y, wdt node enabled in
the JM10 DTS) inherits the running watchdog via WDOG_HW_RUNNING and
keeps it fed until systemd takes over (RuntimeWatchdogSec=10), so a
healthy boot is never reset.

Not armed on the download-mode path: setup_download_mode() runs earlier
in board_late_init() and never returns when VOL+ is held, so
rk_board_late_init() never executes. Paths that run long AFTER this
point (fastboot, recovery) would reset ~89 s in - use MaskROM flashing
instead.

Signed-off-by: John Doe <john.doe@somewhere.on.planet>
---
 board/rockchip/evb_rk3588/evb_rk3588.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/rockchip/evb_rk3588/evb_rk3588.c b/board/rockchip/evb_rk3588/evb_rk3588.c
index 0f1e2d3c4b5..a1b2c3d4e5f 100644
--- a/board/rockchip/evb_rk3588/evb_rk3588.c
+++ b/board/rockchip/evb_rk3588/evb_rk3588.c
@@ -178,3 +178,41 @@ void do_board_download(void)
 	else
 		printf("JM10: crashlog dumped, pull it with: rkdeveloptool rl 0x2000 0x700\n");
 }
+
+/*
+ * Arm the DW watchdog (WDT0 @ 0xfeaf0000, 24 MHz tick) before booting the
+ * kernel, so an early kernel hang (e.g. PCIe3.0 probe) ends in a warm
+ * reset instead of a dead board. Warm resets preserve DDR and the
+ * ramoops/pstore log at 0x110000, which do_board_download() above copies
+ * to eMMC. The kernel DW watchdog driver inherits the running watchdog
+ * and keeps it fed (WATCHDOG_CORE, WDOG_HW_RUNNING) until systemd takes
+ * over, so a healthy boot is not reset.
+ *
+ * Not armed on the download-mode path (VOL+ held): setup_download_mode()
+ * runs earlier in board_late_init() and never returns. Long-running
+ * U-Boot paths entered after this point (fastboot/recovery) would reset
+ * ~89s in; use MaskROM flashing instead.
+ *
+ * TORR = 15 => 2^(16+15) / 24 MHz ~= 89 s.
+ */
+#define JM10_CRU_BASE		0xfd7c0000
+#define JM10_CRU_CLKGATE_CON15	(JM10_CRU_BASE + 0x800 + 15 * 4)
+#define JM10_WDT0_BASE		0xfeaf0000
+#define JM10_WDT_CR		0x00
+#define JM10_WDT_TORR		0x04
+#define JM10_WDT_CRR		0x0c
+
+int rk_board_late_init(void)
+{
+	/* Ungate PCLK_WDT0 (bit0) and TCLK_WDT0 (bit1). */
+	writel(readl(JM10_CRU_CLKGATE_CON15) & ~0x3, JM10_CRU_CLKGATE_CON15);
+
+	/* Reset mode (RMOD=0), enabled, max timeout. */
+	writel(0xff, JM10_WDT0_BASE + JM10_WDT_TORR);
+	writel(0x1, JM10_WDT0_BASE + JM10_WDT_CR);
+	writel(0x76, JM10_WDT0_BASE + JM10_WDT_CRR);
+
+	printf("JM10: watchdog armed (~89s) before booting kernel\n");
+
+	return 0;
+}
